#====================================================================
# E228 - std::polar negative radius is not portable
#====================================================================

id:                     E306
trigger_tool:           clang|clang++|c++
phase:                  runtime|testing
error_signature:        std::polar.*negative|polar=nan,nan|Pole to add is NaN

severity:               2
category:               cpp-polar-negative-radius
match_keywords:         std::polar, negative rho, negative radius, NaN, Pole to add is NaN, libc++, HarmonyOS
title:                  Replace negative-radius std::polar calls with explicit complex components

root_cause:             The C++ std::polar contract requires a non-negative finite radius. Passing a negative radius has undefined behavior; libstdc++ may return the expected finite components while HarmonyOS libc++ returns NaN components.
affected_scope:         Portable C++ DSP, geometry, and signal-processing code that encodes a sign by passing a negative rho value to std::polar.
verification_cmd:       Compile and run a minimal std::polar(-2.0, pi/2) probe with both libstdc++ and HarmonyOS libc++, then rerun the affected API tests on HarmonyOS PC.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           construct-complex-components
rec_description:        Preserve the intended signed complex value by constructing rho*cos(theta) and rho*sin(theta) explicitly, or normalize the sign into a pi angle offset before calling std::polar.
rec_command:            Replace std::polar(rho, theta) for negative rho with complex_t(rho * cos(theta), rho * sin(theta)).
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      normalize-radius-and-angle
fallback_description:   Call std::polar(-rho, theta + pi) when rho is negative, after accounting for angle normalization and type precision.
fallback_command:       rho < 0 ? std::polar(-rho, theta + pi) : std::polar(rho, theta)
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       std::polar\s*\(\s*-[^,]+,
forbid_1_reason:        A negative rho violates the portable std::polar precondition even if one standard library happens to tolerate it.
forbid_1_consequence:   Other standard-library implementations can produce NaN poles or coordinates and fail at runtime.

principles:             
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

